# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lesson structure {#lesson-structure}"
msgstr "Struktur pelajaran {#lesson-structure}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each lesson will include:\n"
"- An introduction including the learning objective for this lesson\n"
"- Detail on the cryptography topic being presented including:\n"
"  - An explanation of the the topic and current algorithms\n"
"  - Math explanations and examples. Some of these are in collapsible sections so you can skip if you do not wish to understand the math detail.\n"
"  - Optional Python code examples that can be run (you will need to be logged in)\n"
"  - Risks from classical computing algorithms\n"
"  - Risks from quantum computing algorithms\n"
"  - Approaches to mitigate this risk\n"
"- A list of key takeaways from the lesson\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap pelajaran akan merangkumi:\n"
"- Pengenalan termasuk objektif pembelajaran untuk pelajaran ini\n"
"- Butiran mengenai topik kriptografi yang dibentangkan termasuk:\n"
"  - Penjelasan tentang topik dan algoritma semasa\n"
"  - Penjelasan dan contoh matematik. Sesetengah daripada ini berada dalam bahagian boleh runtuh supaya anda boleh langkau jika tidak ingin memahami perincian matematik.\n"
"  - Contoh kod Python pilihan yang boleh dijalankan (anda perlu log masuk)\n"
"  - Risiko daripada algoritma pengkomputeran klasik\n"
"  - Risiko daripada algoritma pengkomputeran kuantum\n"
"  - Pendekatan untuk mengurangkan risiko ini\n"
"- Senarai pengambilan utama daripada pelajaran\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Running the Python examples {#running-the-python-examples}"
msgstr "Menjalankan contoh Python {#running-the-python-examples}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Python code has been run already so that readers browsing the text can "
"see the results without additional steps. However, and in particular for "
"those with an interest in software development, you are encouraged to run "
"these examples yourself. You can also experiment with input parameters and "
"explore the principles in an experimental way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod Python telah dijalankan terlebih dahulu supaya pembaca yang melayari "
"teks boleh melihat hasilnya tanpa langkah tambahan. Namun begitu, "
"terutamanya bagi mereka yang berminat dalam pembangunan perisian, anda "
"digalakkan untuk menjalankan contoh-contoh ini sendiri. Anda juga boleh "
"bereksperimen dengan parameter input dan meneroka prinsip dengan cara "
"eksperimen.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you run a Python cell for the first time, you will be prompted to log "
"in to IBM Quantum&reg;.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila anda menjalankan sel Python buat pertama kali, anda akan diminta "
"untuk log masuk ke IBM Quantum&reg;.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should run each Python cell in order, from the beginning of the "
"notebook. Later cells are typically dependent on earlier ones to set up "
"libraries, variables, and so on. Each cell has been written to produce some "
"output after execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda harus menjalankan setiap sel Python mengikut urutan, dari permulaan "
"buku nota. Sel kemudian biasanya bergantung pada sel sebelumnya untuk "
"menyediakan perpustakaan, pemboleh ubah, dan sebagainya. Setiap sel telah "
"ditulis untuk menghasilkan beberapa output selepas pelaksanaan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"The Python code examples are provided to demonstrate the mathematical principles of the algorithms being discussed. They are not intended to be used as actual implementations. It is essential to use well-supported and reviewed security libraries in any real-world usage.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Penting\">\n"
"Contoh kod Python disediakan untuk menunjukkan prinsip matematik algoritma yang dibincangkan. Ia tidak bertujuan untuk digunakan sebagai pelaksanaan sebenar. Adalah penting untuk menggunakan perpustakaan keselamatan yang disokong dan disemak dengan baik dalam sebarang penggunaan dunia sebenar.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

